WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.060
Ka...

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:03.360
Kaori...

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.660
Sou-kun?

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.230
Wh-What are you doing?

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.340
Huh? What am I...?

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.990
Oh! No, no, no! Nothing!
I didn't do anything!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.950
I found this person
on the ground here!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:15.760
What?

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.120
Uh, um...

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.980
It looks like she's breathing, at least.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.390
Uh, what should we do?

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.040
Um, maybe we'd better call an ambulance?

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.580
Or no, get a teacher first?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.550
Um...

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.930
Sou...

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.040
Do you know her?

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.760
I don't! Honest!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.160
Then how...

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.310
Um...

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.810
Do you know me?

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.880
Do you... know me...?

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.820
Um, what's your name?

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:52.540
What's your name...

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.140
Yui...

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.100
My name...

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.580
is Furukawa Yui.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.260
W-Wait!

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.960
F-Furukawa-san?!

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.520
She was naked and didn't know anything except her name?

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.800
What's up with that?

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.940
Maybe she got caught up in some sort of incident?

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.860
More like, this screams of something illicit.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.820
It's okay. You can come in.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.070
I'm so glad we had your uniform, Airi-chan.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.410
I keep it on hand just for emergencies like these.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.780
Not for when you go on a rampage?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:05.910
No!

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.160
Why do I have to get treated like I'm this wild child?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.930
Well, if the shoe fits...

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.170
Knock it off.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.950
Going on rampages at school and changing out of dirty uniforms...

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.370
What kinda person do you take me for?

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.800
Huh? What?

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:21.800
Huh?

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.540
Um...

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.420
Do you two know each other?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.310
What? I don't know her at all!

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.730
She called me by name earlier.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.330
Hey, isn't there anything else you can say?

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.140
Nothing at all?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.000
This really isn't something we can handle by ourselves.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.760
Maybe we should talk to the police—

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.720
Huh? What?

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.840
Hey!

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:00.540
Sleepy.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.840
What the...

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:04.920
Well, for now...

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:09.530
I'll take her home with me,
at least for today, and see how things go.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.680
Okay.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.070
You're awake, I see.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.350
What... month and day is it today?

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.910
Huh? It's October 1st.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.380
The 1st?

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.140
Still the 1st...

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.340
What's wrong?

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.380
Are you okay?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.880
I have to go... to Uchihama Academy.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.890
Not this late at night. We'll go tomorrow.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:47.990
Okay?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.020
Come in.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.670
How may I be of service?

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.550
There are a couple things I want you to arrange for me.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.630
What? Naked?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.990
And she had amnesia?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.580
I don't know, she was a strange girl, wasn't she?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.260
I hope she isn't caught up in anything bad.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.800
Well, I'm sure Nagisa-senpai will handle it somehow.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.000
This curry's way better than the one I usually make.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.390
What? Is it?

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.510
Is there something different in it?

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.290
You're so oblivious, Sou-kun.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.260
It's homemade, from the roux on up.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.020
Okay, Furukawa-san, you can sit there.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.180
Make her feel welcome, everyone.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.480
I'm Fukasawa Karin.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.360
Nice to meet you.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.280
I am pleased to meet you.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.280
She's a transfer student?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.280
Due to start today?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.260
That's right.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:53.790
Isn't it?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.110
Does that mean you got your memories back?

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.000
No...

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.260
Yesterday...

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.450
Why were you, uh, naked?

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.450
I do not know.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.180
Well, that aside...

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:12.000
I'll be taking care of her at my place for a while,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.180
so don't worry.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.280
Right.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.220
Whoa, what?

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.830
Furukawa-san, are you okay
coming to school in your condition?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.480
I felt like I had to come here,
to Uchihama Academy.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.360
What?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:31.790
This place...

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.920
What do you do here?

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:34.800
What?

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.940
Uh...

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.540
This is the Astronomy Club, but...

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.320
The "Astronomy" is in name only, really.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:42.920
It's not <i>supposed</i> to be.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.710
We kick back, have fun,

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.310
go on the occasional rampage...

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:50.960
There's laughter, and tears, and violence...

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:53.260
That doesn't explain anything.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.930
Do you have any interest in the stars?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.560
We're planning to build a planetarium for the school festival.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.940
A planetarium...

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.680
Yup. We'll build a huge dome
and project a whole swath of stars inside.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:09.670
We'll have our own starry sky
right here in this room!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.820
You are going to make a sky full of stars here?

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.480
Well, something like that.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.040
How are you going to make it?

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:22.000
First, we need to decide on
what to make the dome out of.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.750
Uh, let's see, and then... Um...

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.130
Would you like to help too, Yui-san?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.130
Yes.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.840
Then I guess that makes you a provisional club member.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.010
Glad to have you!

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.210
Testing, testing. Can you hear me?

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.900
Are we good?

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.010
This is much higher than I thought.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.300
Will they have a blackout curtain this big?

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.600
I'll go look.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:54.530
How about you guys?

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:57.030
What? Oh, almost done.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.700
Is this spot about right?

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.600
Yeah... Maybe a bit more this way?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.130
Oh, there's no brush.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.250
I'll pop out and see if I can
borrow one from somewhere.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.800
See you la... ter?

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.420
Yui-san, you don't need to go.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.390
Mind helping me out over here?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.010
U-Um...

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:19.860
Huh?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.690
Looks like you got rejected.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.070
Has she gotten attached to Airi and Sou?

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.750
Something like that.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.500
Furukawa-san?

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.010
Furukawa-san.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.460
What are you doing out here?

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.700
I wanted to get some sunlight.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.530
It's almost time for class.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.990
Yes.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.380
Though I do not understand it very well.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.040
Oh, is that so?

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:30.810
I feel there is something else
that I ought to be doing.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.610
This might sound irresponsible,

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:35.100
but for the moment,

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.880
why don't you just try to enjoy what's going on right now?

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:41.560
Look, making a sky full of stars
sounds like fun, right?

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.060
Yes...

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.120
That poker face isn't very convincing.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.090
Is something the matter?

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.660
What? Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:14.340
Alexander's eastern expedition
took him as far as the Indus Valley,

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.820
but he faced opposition from his men
...and the Achaemenid Persian Empire—

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:21.400
Uh, Furukawa-san? Wait!

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:23.760
I'll go check on her.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.560
Furukawa-san, what's wrong?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.020
Do you feel sick?

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:32.800
Sasaki Kaori... Year 2, Class B...

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.540
You want to see her?

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:35.820
But we're in the middle of class.

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:38.780
Um...

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.360
What... should I...

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.320
Uh...

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.700
This doesn't look good.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.420
What is this?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.140
Has she grown tired of Sou and me already?

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:54.420
I have no clue.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.860
You take this and put five spoonfuls into the pot.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:10:59.380
Okay.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:00.490
Oh...

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.970
Whoa!

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:14.610
Thank you.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.580
Oh?

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.490
Today's cup is wonderfully fragrant.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:25.170
Oh, I tried a blend of teas today.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:28.400
Also, I tried steeping it a little longer than usual.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:29.450
I see.

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:32.710
Oh, how about we also open a café
for the school festival?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.700
That sounds like fun!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:35.960
A planetarium café!

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:41.370
And with Kaori and Nagisa-san as waitresses,
I bet the customers will come in droves!

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.070
I don't know about this.

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:47.140
Sounds like the astronomy part is gonna end up being pushed to the sidelines.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:50.570
I'd like it if we could serve some small baked sweets, too.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.190
Oh, I know! It'd be great if we all had matching uniforms, right?

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:54.100
Yeah, that's true... I guess it's not that big a deal...

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.110
Something like this.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:59.200
That's so cute! I bet you'd look great in it.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:01.240
I'd prefer something a little more mature.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.530
Don't you think that's a bit too bold?

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:06.490
How about something kind of quirky like this?

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.000
Huh? What? No good?

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.460
Oh, have you finished drawing yours, Furukawa-san?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.320
Yes.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:19.960
It's wonderfully avant-garde, Yui-san.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.930
It's not here.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.520
This is a problem.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.080
Hey, I heard that a girl from Class C saw a ghost.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.040
Did you hear? It apparently showed up again.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.970
A lot of people have been reporting sightings lately.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.360
They're probably mistaken, though.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:04.170
Don't you think it's like, totally super scary, for real?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.800
There's no such thing as ghosts.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.520
Nothing to be scared of.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:09.760
You don't have to act all tough.

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:13.230
We'll drop it off here, if you don't mind.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.640
There's a good bit of stuff up here.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:18.940
I've heard there have been weird things happening in this area lately.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.900
You hear a mechanical whine, and then...

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.510
A bunch of boxes suddenly fall down,

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.360
or people get dizzy and collapse.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.400
And one moment,

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.590
you hear the windows going rattle-rattle, rattle-rattle, and before you know it...

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.530
Smash!

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:36.500
Eep.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:42.800
Or so the rumors say.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.090
Say what exactly?

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.550
O-Oh, did that scare you too, Furukawa-san?

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.720
It was a bit of a shock to hear her yell like that, right?

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.560
Kaori, give it a break.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:56.480
But it's true. There's been a lot of weird rumors lately.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.870
I also heard this story about people suddenly falling asleep in the vicinity of the school.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.730
Hey, what's that sound?

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.650
It's... not the elevator, is it?

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.390
H-Hey!

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:16.160
Watch out!

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:28.090
Ow.

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.350
Nicely done, Akiyama-san.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.100
Thanks.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.190
Ew, it's the student council president.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.850
What do you mean, "ew"?

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.250
I've come to you, the Astronomy Club,

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.160
with a formal request from the student council.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:48.570
We've got a lot on our plates too with
the school festival coming up, you know.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.640
That's right. We'd like to focus on preparations.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.680
This happens every year,

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:58.360
but minor squabbles between students
are especially common at around this time.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:02.090
Therefore, we'd like you to smooth over any scuffles the Disciplinary Committee can't handle

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:04.090
from now until the end of the festival.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.150
Really? Well, I sure can't wait to take them on.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:09.050
Keep things as peaceful as possible, all right?

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.310
And one other thing.

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:15.280
There's a rumor about a ghost
that's been spreading like wildfire lately.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.460
You've heard of it too, right?

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:20.140
I want you to investigate that matter.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.040
Whether it's just a wild rumor
or someone playing a practical joke,

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.420
the students being needlessly frightened
is detrimental to the discipline we maintain at this school.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.110
Have you gained a new club member?

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:33.820
We have. She's a transfer student.

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:36.630
Is that... right...

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:42.410
What are we going to do about this ghost investigation thing?

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.510
It sounds like fun!

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.910
I say we start by questioning
eyewitnesses tomorrow

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.840
and investigating the places
where it's been spotted.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:52.300
Ghosts and mysterious accidents...

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:53.870
It's rather unsettling.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:56.280
It'd be nice if we could get it all resolved quickly.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:58.220
Speaking of spooky stories, there's that one...

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.580
about people who suddenly fall asleep, never to wake.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.690
Maybe there's something
otherworldly going on there too.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:08.150
I hear the symptoms have only been observed within the Uchihama city limits.

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.450
And they apparently have no leads on either the cause or the cure.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.820
I wonder what could possibly be happening.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:20.700
Oh!

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:23.150
Furukawa-san!

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:25.790
Fukasawa-san, good morning.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:28.280
What's up? Aren't you going to the classroom?

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:29.100
Right...

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:31.670
Come on! It's this way.

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:34.890
All right! Time to decide our ghostbusting partners.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.740
Please draw one.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.970
Hey! Howdy, partner!

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:43.270
Let's go all-out and catch that Japanese ghost!

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.230
I think you'd spook even a ghost with that.

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.240
All right, time to draw!

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:51.440
It's Kaori.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.700
I'll do my best not to slow you down.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:56.950
You saw it clearly?

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.930
Would you mind telling us what you remember?

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:00.930
Okay.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.960
It was in the storage area on the fifth floor.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.290
I went to the back after going up the stairs

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.960
to get some materials for the school festival.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.000
I didn't think there was anyone there,

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.330
but then I sensed a presence, and...

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:15.790
You didn't <i>have</i> to come along, you know.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:16.820
I'm fine.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:22.960
Hey, Sou-kun, you really don't know Furukawa-san, right?

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.470
Nope, not at all.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.440
Right, of course.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.760
Yeah, sorry. Don't mind me.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:31.400
But she's a strange girl, isn't she?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:33.450
Yeah.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:38.070
Huh? It won't turn on.

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:40.220
I guess we'll just have to go in like this.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.080
What could this thing be?

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.560
It's kind of suspicious.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:48.920
Let's take a quick look.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:54.910
H-Hey...

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.060
Oh!

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:57.550
S-Sorry.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:01.010
A lot of the eyewitness accounts mentioned this area.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:03.070
Well, it's always dimly lit,

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.370
so people could easily have mistaken what they saw, but...

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.910
Furukawa-san, would you go check things out over there?

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:08.790
Okay.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.240
When I turned around,
a girl was walking straight toward me.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.850
She was all shimmery,
and I could see right through her.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:24.080
It was really scary.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.510
Anything distinctive
about the way she looked?

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:29.740
She was wearing our school's uniform
and had long hair.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.440
So, to sum up,

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:35.630
most people reported the ghost as
having long hair and wearing a uniform.

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:39.100
The fact that the eyewitness accounts are consistent means that,

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:41.040
whether it's truly a ghost or not,

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.770
there actually was some
ghost-like figure that they saw.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:47.710
I get the feeling that if we questioned more people,

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.440
we'd only end up with more similar accounts.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.620
I'd say so.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.890
In any case, let's move on
to preparing for the school festival.

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:55.820
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:56.830
That reminds me.

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:58.780
The aforementioned items have come in.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.820
The aforementioned items?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.490
Ooh!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.010
Woohoo!

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.890
They turned out quite nicely for a rush order.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:10.170
Man, oh, man!

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:13.030
We're gonna be mobbed
with or without the planetarium!

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:15.000
What are you doing?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.470
Imagining Jennifer wearing one of those outfits.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:19.820
Huh.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.900
Airi-san, we're next.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:23.470
What? Oh, o-okay.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.970
Ooh!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.150
I feel like Nagisa-senpai is being a little bit spiteful.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:35.200
Jesus! Why didn't God create everyone to be equal?!

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.780
I'm still growing, okay?!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:39.900
A-Airi-chan, you're cute,
and smart, and good at sports,

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.920
so even if you're a little on the lean side...

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:44.650
I mean, don't let it bother you!

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.530
Forget it already!

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:46.540
Here.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:49.600
Well?

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.920
It feels really soft and nice.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:55.920
Now, this one.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:56.920
Here.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:58.660
Well?

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:00.760
It feels lacking.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.290
You all suck!

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:03.860
Why don't you just come out and say that they're small?!

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:04.860
S-Stop!

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:05.330
Why don't you just come out and say that they're small?!

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.760
Airi-chan!

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:13.810
It looks like Kaori-san's design
should be more universally flattering.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:16.490
The other one would be too provocative.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.030
It seems to provoke fights, too.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:18.940
You better believe it.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.360
Well? Are you starting to get used
to the Astronomy Club?

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.410
It's a bit of an odd group, but...

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.420
Yes, somewhat.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.640
Sasaki-san, and Hasekura-san,

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.750
and Hanamiya-san,
and Akiyama-san, and Kenny-san...

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:36.660
You all get rowdy and laugh together,
and that is the Astronomy Club.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.170
Am I correct?

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.340
Yup. It's pretty much like this every day.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:42.490
Every day...

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:44.200
Oh? Yui-san, where's your hat?

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:44.760
Oh...

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.470
Maybe you left it behind when you were changing.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:49.420
I will go get it.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.840
I'm not sure if Yui-san will be all right on her own, so I'll go with her.

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:58.410
See you all tomorrow.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:20.700
Yui-san.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.170
Did you find your hat?

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:26.090
Yes. I'm sorry for holding you up.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:31.330
Today is October 7th, right?

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:33.750
It is, but... what happened?

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.850
You seem different somehow.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:37.280
I figured it out.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.440
The reason I am here.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:40.070
What?

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.180
What is it? What do you mean?

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:26.500
Hey, do you remember?

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:27.580
That was amazing, Hasekura-san!

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:28.600
We're springing into action!

00:23:28.600 --> 00:23:29.180
Just give in.

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:29.900
It looks like you're having fun, Prez.

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:30.860
Because I interfered...

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:32.520
Do something about those barbarians!

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.620
It's dangerous!

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:39.180
Episode three: "The President Dreams with Sparkling Eyes."
